      {
        "parameters": {
          "promptType": "define",
          "text": "=Find this metric in the {{ $json.company }} 2025-26 annual report.\n\nCompany: {{ $json.company }}\nMetric: {{ $json.metrics.metric }}\nDefinition: {{ $json.metrics.description }}\nExpected unit: {{ $json.metrics.unit }}\n\nUse the annual_report_search tool. Include the company name and the metric in your search query.\n\nRules:\n- Use ONLY numbers that appear in the search results for {{ $json.company }}. Never guess or use outside knowledge.\n- For money amounts, prefer CONSOLIDATED figures over standalone figures.\n- Convert Indian number format to plain digits: 6,17,437 becomes 617437.\n- Give the value in the expected unit. Percentages as plain numbers (12.5 means 12.5%).\n- page = the page number from the metadata of the source you used.\n- evidence = a short exact quote of the line that contains the number.\n- If the value is not in the search results, set found to false and value and page to null.\n\nRespond in JSON only, exactly like this:\n{\"found\": true, \"value\": 617437, \"page\": 108, \"evidence\": \"Total employees 6,17,437\"}",
          "options": {
            "maxIterations": 5
          }
        },
